  "body": "I'm not sure if this should go in this repo, the CSSWG repo, or some other place. Feel free to direct me to the correct place to bring this up.\r\n\r\nOn Chrome and Firefox (probably Safari as well), there appears to be an inconsistency in the way certain CSS colors are parsed between canvas styles (e.g. setting `fillStyle` and `strokeStyle`) and stylesheets.\r\n\r\nWhen setting the canvas' fill/stroke style, `rgb()`/`rgba()` and `hsl()`/`hsla()` color values with missing close-parentheses such as `rgb(255, 0, 0` are considered valid. In stylesheets, however, they are not.\r\n\r\nAs mentioned, this seems to happen across browsers (Chrome and Firefox; I don't own a Mac so no Safari but it also happened on Midori, another WebKit-based browser), but I can't find this mentioned anywhere in the spec.\r\n\r\nHere's a demo: [color-parse-difference.html.zip](https://github.com/whatwg/html/files/5684232/color-parse-difference.html.zip)\r\n",
